The Awami League put into effect their plans spelt out as
under:
(a) denial of all logistical support to the Armed Forces;
(b) disruption of all troop movements;
(c) disruption of water and power supplies to all Cantonments;
(d) stopping all civilian employees from working for the
Armed Forces. 
|
Mujib declared: ‘Pakistan as it stands is finished.

On 14 March Bhutto suggested two Prime Ministers, he himself
for West Pakistan and Mujib for East Pakistan, and his utterances,
e.g., Udhar tum, idhar hum, clearly meant two Pakistans.

Battle exhaustion is something which only those who have
hee a considerable time—several months—under fire can
} understand.

